<h1>Local server internals</h1>
<p class="lede">The Local edition's backend: a single Node.js process on your own computer that serves the page, talks to Jira with your API token, and runs JARVIS in the background.</p>

<h2>What starts when you run <code>npm start</code></h2>
<ol class="steps-list">
  <li><code>tsc</code> compiles <code>src/</code> into <code>dist/</code>.</li>
  <li><code>node dist/server/index.js</code> starts an HTTP server on <code>127.0.0.1:4545</code> (only your own computer can reach it).</li>
  <li><code>monitor.start()</code> schedules the first JARVIS check 1.5 seconds later, then every 60 seconds.</li>
  <li>It prints which credentials it uses: environment variables or <code>~/.jira-bug-dashboard/config.json</code>.</li>
</ol>

